Defects found:

- Line 77: input `index.html='<html><a href="x.html">x</a></html>'`, `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json={}`. Consequence: both anchors are absent, `seg` becomes empty, and line 143 returns success after a zero-page audit.

- Line 79: input cardiology segment `<a href="heart-failure.html">HF</a>`. Consequence: the selector rejects hyphenated page names, so that page is invisible to the count.

- Line 92: input page HTML `<!-- AUTO_INCLUDE_TRIAL_IDS removed from seed -->` padded past 10000 bytes, with no actual seed array. Consequence: the guard is satisfied by its own marker text and skips a page the object reader should inspect.

- Line 89: input indexed page `x.html` of 9999 bytes with valid `PAGE_MAP["x.html"]` and a valid object. Consequence: the page is silently dropped from all buckets, so the denominator excludes an audited target.

- Line 101: input object `{"inputs":{"trials":[{"nct":"unknown","registration":"NCT12345678"}]}}`. Consequence: the invalid nonempty `nct` field shadows the valid `registration`, causing a real trial ID to be discarded.

- Lines 111 and 120: input cache `{"NCT00000001":{"error":"timeout"}}` and object `{"inputs":{"trials":[{"nct":"NCT00000001"}]}}`. Consequence: a total fetch failure leaves `without=[]`, so the page is classified as `FINE`.

- Line 123: input cache `{"NCT1":{"title":"","primary":["Antibody titer"],"secondary":[],"other":[]},"NCT2":{"error":"timeout"}}` and object containing both IDs. Consequence: it reports `ALL ... k=2` although only one trial was actually classified.

- Lines 27-32: input `has_clinical({"primary":["Overall survival"],"secondary":[],"other":[]})`. Consequence: a standard clinical endpoint is missed because the efficacy selector lacks `survival`.

No finding from this packet alone: CRLF/LF text comparison, merged-cell handling, or worktree-vs-HEAD-vs-served copy mismatch.
